<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan money rates end up on funds shortage.</title>
<headline>Pakistan money rates end up on funds shortage.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's inter-bank money market rates closed higher on Sunday amid a shortage of funds. Dealers said rates were likely to remain steady at current levels on Monday.</p>
<p>Overnight funds opened at 13 percent but soon moved up and closed at 17 percent, a dealer at KASB &amp; Co said.</p>
<p>The dealers said rates were unlikely to change as no major inflow or outflow was expected in the next few sessions.</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
